/*
  StatusBar.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0182 · StatusBar (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Keys mirror the web source
  (components/layout/StatusBar.tsx + its six ./status-bar/ segment children) VERBATIM — every `t(key,
  default)` call across the bar + its segments — so each Swift literal routes through the facade fallback and
  the sources hold no hardcoded English. `{{age}}` / `{{count}}` / `{{uptime}}` slots are filled by
  StatusBarInterpolation (the native peer of i18next interpolation).

  A small set of keys have no literal web string because the web bar performs no fetch of its own (the data
  states live in the segments); the native peer surfaces the orthogonal P4 state chips + a loading skeleton +
  a friendly empty descriptor, so each gets a localizable key here.

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept
  in a per-surface table ("StatusBar") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings.
*/

